    "ls|LS17_S3_U_138": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 138 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 11.02.2020 \nPMGSY IN KERALA \n \n*138.  SHRI M.K. RAGHAVAN: \n \nWill the Minister of  RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the details of roads identified for developmen t under the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sadak \nYojana (PMGSY) in Kozhikode, in particular and other districts of Kerala, in general; \n(b)  the total funds sanctioned, spent and un-spent  under the scheme during the last three years \nparticularly in Kozhikode district and in the State of Kerala, in general; and \n(c)  the manner in which the Government proposes to  speed up the road connectivity? \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n(a) to (c): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (c) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *138  \ndue for answer on 11.02.2020  \n \n(a): The State of Kerala has been sanctioned its fu ll entitlement under Pradhan Mantri Gram \nSadak Yojana (PMGSY)-I and PMGSY-II.  Details of district-wise roads sanctioned and \ncompleted under PMGSY-I and PMGSY-II including Kozh ikode district of Kerala is at \nAnnexure. Under PMGSY-III, 1425 km road length has been allocated to the State of Kerala and \nthe state has initiated planning activities for road identification.  \n \n(b):  The total funds sanctioned, utilized and unspent under PMGSY during the last three years in \nthe State of Kerala and Kozhikode district are as under:- \n (In Rs Crore) \n* Funds are sanctioned to each district (PIUs) based on their actual fund request. \n \n \n(c): The progress of implementation of rural roads under PMGSY is regularly monitored by way \nof Regional Review Meetings (RRMs), Performance Rev iew Committee (PRC) Meetings, Pre-\nEmpowered/Empowered Committee Meetings, Video Conference with the State. At District level, \nthe District Development Coordination and Monitorin g Committee (Disha) headed by a Member \nof Parliament (LS) monitors the implementation of v arious schemes of Government of India \nincluding PMGSY. In addition to this, special revie w meetings are also held by Secretary/ \nAdditional Secretary/ Joint Secretary, Ministry of Rural Development with Chief Secretaries/ \nPrincipal Secretaries of the States.  \n \n***** \n  \nYear  Fund sanctioned to \nState \n(Central Share & \nState Share) \nFund \nUtilized \n(State) \nFund  \nun-spent \n(State) \nFund \nsanctioned to \nKozhikode* \nFund Utilized \nby \nKozhikode* \n2016 -17  305.67  267.43  38.24  18.98  18.98  \n2017-18 280.19 206.09 74.10 13.30 13.30 \n2018-19 162.92 225.16 0 10.28 10.28 \n\nANNEXURE \nAnnexure referred to in part (a) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No. *138 to be answered on 11.02.2020 \n \n  PMGSY-I \nSr.No.  District Name No of \nRoadwork \nSanctioned  \nRoad \nLength \nSanctioned  \nNo of \nBridge \nWork \nSanctioned  \nNo of \nRoad \nWork \nCompleted  \nNo of \nBridge \nWorks \nCompleted  \nRoad \nLength \nCompleted  \nBalance \nRoad \nLength \n1 Alappuzha 71 101.008 0 66 0 90.666 7.915 \n2 Ernakulam  65  130.695  1 65  1 130.318  0.000  \n3 Idukki 112 401.094 0 104 0 375.083 26.183 \n4 Kannur  131  367.308  0 127  0 353.320  11.836  \n5 Kasaragod 96 247.091 0 93 0 239.030 7.700 \n6 Kollam  78  166.137  0 78  0 165.962  0.000  \n7 Kottayam 62 153.448 0 55 0 128.157 23.409 \n8 Kozhikode 131 289.146 0 126 0 271.523 17.670 \n9 Malappuram 136 344.148 0 136 0 338.265 0.000 \n10 Palakkad 86 278.810 0 79 0 250.672 21.849 \n11 Pathanamthitta 78 186.627 0 75 0 174.127 8.000 \n12 Thiruvananthapuram  177 292.752 0 171 0 275.436 17.130 \n13 Thrissur 114 233.294 0 113 0 229.152 3.420 \n14 Wayanad 43 136.004 0 37 0 116.422 17.932 \n Total: 1,380 3,327.562 1 1,325 1 3,138.133 163.044  \n  \n \n\n PMGSY-II \nSr.No.  District Name No of \nRoadwork \nSanctioned \nRoad \nLength \n