    "ls|LS17_S3_U_139": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 139 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 11.02.2020 \nIMPLEMENTATION OF PMAY-G \n \n*139.  SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH JOSHI: \nSHRI RAVINDRA KUSHWAHA: \n \nWill the Minister of  RURAL DEVELOPMENT \n be pleased to state: \n \n(a)  the target for construction of houses in rural  areas under Pradhan Mantri Awas \nYojana-Gramin (PMAY-G) till 2022; \n(b)  whether targets under PMAY-G are being achieve d in the country and if so, the \ndetails thereof, State-wise; \n(c)  the details of the financial assistance provid ed under the scheme at present; \n(d)  whether the Government is considering to incre ase the amount of assistance being \nprovided for the construction of houses under PMAY- G, if so, the details thereof and \nif not, the reasons therefor; \n(e)  whether any scheme to broaden the eligibility list of Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana is \nunder consideration of the Government and if so, the details thereof; \n(f)  the details of the number of housing units con structed under PMAY-G so far, State-\nwise and year-wise; and \n(g)  the time by which the remaining housing units are targeted to be constructed? \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n(a) to (g): A statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n  \n\nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PART (a) to (g) OF LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO.*139 TO BE ANSWERED ON 11.02.2020 REGAR DING \nIMPLEMENTATION OF PMAY-G \n \n(a): To achieve the objective of “Housing for All” by 2022, the Ministry of Rural \nDevelopment is implementing Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yo jana – Gramin (PMAY-G) w.e.f. 1 \nst  \nApril, 2016 with a target for construction of 2.95 crore houses in rural areas by 2022. \n \n(b): State/ UT-wise targets and achievements under PMAY-G are at Annexure I.  \n \n(c) and (d): Under PMAY-G, beneficiaries are provid ed an enhanced unit assistance of Rs. \n1.20 lakh in plains (which was Rs. 70,000 under the  erstwhile Indira Awaas Yojana) and Rs. \n1.30 lakh in hilly states, difficult areas and Inte grated Action Plan (IAP) districts (which was \nRs. 75,000 under the erstwhile Indira Awaas Yojana)  for construction of a pucca house. In \naddition, there is provision of 90/95 persondays of  unskilled labour wages through \nconvergence with Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Empl oyment Guarantee Scheme \n(MGNREGS) and Rs. 12,000 for construction of toilet  through convergence with Swachh \nBharat Mission – Gramin (SBM-G), MGNREGS or any oth er dedicated source of \nfunding. At present, there is no proposal for enhancing the unit assistance under PMAY-G. \n  \n(e): For households, who though eligible as per the  provisions of the scheme, could not be \nincluded in the Permanent Wait List (PWL) of PMAY-G prepared on the basis of SECC 2011 \ndata, an exercise was conducted across the country for identifying such households and \ncapturing their details through the mobile applicat ion “Awaas+”. A total of 3.67 crore \nhouseholds has been uploaded on Awaas+ from across the country. The Ministry has \nconstituted an Expert Committee for analysis of “Awaas+” data. \n \n(f): State/UT-wise and year-wise number of houses c onstructed under PMAY-G, as on \n06.02.2020, are given in Annexure II. \n \n(g): The remaining houses are targeted for construction by 2022. \n \n********  \n\nAnnexure I \n \nANNEXURE REFERRED IN STATEMENT IN REPLY TO PART (b)  OF LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION NO.*139 TO BE ANSWERED ON 11 .02.2020 \nREGARDING IMPLEMENTATION OF PMAY-G \nStates/UT-wise target, number of houses sanctioned and completed under PMAY-G, as on \n06.02.2020  \nS. \nNo. State Name Phase I (2016-17 to 2018-19) Phase II (2019-20) \nTarget Sanctioned  Completed  Target Sanctioned  Completed  \n1 \nARUNACHAL \nPRADESH 11221 \n 2528  156  7500  421  0 \n2 ASSAM 259814  235608  202524  256043  166375  14632  \n3 BIHAR  1176617  1133362  790498  101