    "ls|LS17_S3_U_249": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 249  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 11.03.2020 \n    \nCRITERIA FOR RECRUITMENT \n*249. SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH CHOUDHARY: \n \n  Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the details of the total number of recruitments  made by the Railways \nthrough the Railway Recruitment Board during the last three years;   \n(b) whether there is any region/State -wise criteria for recruitment in \nIndian Railways through Railway Recruitment Board and if so, the \ndetails thereof; \n \n(c)the details of the recruitment exams that have not been conducted \nduring last year despite issuing notifications therefor; \n(d)the reasons for not conducting the exams despite issue of notification \nof exam for Non -Technical Popular Categories (NTPC) Group and \nGroup ‘D’ and action taken to start conducting these exams on time; \nand \n(e)the total number of people from the State of Jharkhand who joined \nthe Indian Railways during the last three years? \n \n \n \n \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS AND COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n \n(SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n \n \n(a) to (e): A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (e ) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 2 49 BY SHRI CHANDRA PRAKASH CHOUDHARY  TO BE \nANSWERED IN LOK SABHA ON 11.03.2020 REGARDING CRITERIA FOR \nRECRUITMENT  \n(a): During the last three years i.e. 2017 -2018 to 2019 -2020 (upto \n05.03.2020), a total number of 1,47,620 candidates have been \nempanelled for various Group ‘C’ posts (including Level -1) by Railways \nthrough Railway Recruitment Boards (RRBs)  and Railway Recruitment \nCells (RRCs).  \n  \n(b): No, Sir.  Indian Railways is an organization having pan India \ncharacter. Candidates are free to apply to any RRB throughout the \ncountry in response to the advertisements.  \n \n(c): Three recruitment examinations against Centralized Employment \nNotifications (CEN) No. 01 /2019 for Non-Technical Popular Categories \n(NTPC) Group, CEN No. 03/2019 for Ministerial & Isolated Categories and \nCEN No. RRC -01/2019 for Level -1 posts (erstwhile Group ‘D’), are in \nprocess to be conducted in the coming months.   \n \n(d): To fix Examination Conducting Agency (ECA)  against CEN No. \n01/2019 and 03/2019, open tenders have been floated. After fixing of ECA, \ndates for the examinations will be announced.  For CEN No. RRC-01/2019, \ntendering process for engaging vendor is under way.  \n \n(e):  A total nu mber of 6551 candidates from Jharkhand have been \nempanelled by all RRBs and RRCs for appointment on Indian \nRailways/Production Units during the last three years. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_25": "O.I.H. \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 25 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 04.02.2020 \nPRADHAN MANTRI GRAM SADAK YOJANA \n \n*25.  SHRIMATI JASKAUR MEENA: \nSHRI NIHAL CHAND: \n \nWill the Minister of RURAL DEVELOPMENT  be pleased to state: \n \n(a) the main features of the Pradhan Mantri Gram Sa dak Yojana (PMGSY); \n(b)  the details of the funds sanctioned, allocated  and utilised under the scheme \nacross the country during the last three years and the current year, State-wise, \nincluding Rajasthan; \n(c)  the details of the rural road projects sanctio ned in Rajasthan during the said \nperiod and the present status thereof; \n(d)  whether the Government has given approval for implementation of phase-III of \nPMGSY in the country; \n(e)  if so, the details thereof including the numbe r of districts proposed to be \nincluded under the same along with the details of f unds to be sanctioned in this \nregard especially for the districts of Dausa and Ganganagar of Rajasthan; and \n(f)  the details of the targets fixed under the sam e?  \n \n \nANSWER  \nMINISTER OF RURAL DEVELOPMENT  \n(SHRI NARENDRA SINGH TOMAR) \n \n \n(a) to (f):   A Statement is laid on the table of the House. \n\nStatement referred to in reply to Parts (a) to (f) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No.25 \ndue for answer on 04.02.2020  \n(a): The Government launched Pradhan Mantri Gram Sa dak Yojana (PMGSY) in December \n2000, as a one-time special intervention to provide  rural connectivity, by way of a single all-\nweather road, to the eligible unconnected habitatio ns of designated population size (500+ in \nplain areas and 250+ in North-Eastern States, Himal ayan States, Deserts and Tribal Areas as \nper 2001 census) in the core network for uplifting the socio-economic condition of the rural \npopulation. In the critical Left Wing Extremism aff ected blocks (as identified by Ministry of \nHome Affairs), additional relaxation has been given  to connect habitations with population \n100 persons and above (2001 census). The Government  subsequently launched new \ninterventions/verticals namely PMGSY-II for upgrada tion of 50,000 Km of road length and \nRoad Connectivity Project for Left Wing Extremism A ffected Areas (RCPLWEA) for \nconstruction/upgradation of strategically important roads.  \n(b): The details of funds sanctioned/allocated and utilised under the scheme across the \ncountry during the last three years and the current  year, State-wise, including Rajasthan is \nplaced at Annexure-I.   \n(c): The State of Rajasthan has been sanctioned its  full entitlement under PMGSY-I and \nPMGSY-II.  The details of rural road projects sanctioned in Ra jasthan during the last three \nyears and the current year and the present status thereof are as indicated below:- \nFinancial Year Proposals Sanctioned Works Completed  \n  No. Length (Km) No. Length (Km) \n2016 -17  1449  4251.34  1439  4213.64  \n2017-18 401 3464.263 384 3336.313 \n2018 -19  - - - - \n2019-20 - - - - \n  \n(d) to (f): The Government has on 10 th  July, 2019 approved phase-III of PMGSY with an aim  \nto consolidate 1,25,000 km Through Routes and Major  Rural Links connecting habitations, \ninter-alia to Gramin Agricultural Markets (GrAMs), Higher Secondary School and Hospitals \nat an estimated cost of Rs 80,250 crore.  The road length allocated to the States under \nPMGSY-III is placed at Annexure-II . The State of Rajasthan has been allocated 8,662.5  km \nunder PMGSY-III. As reported by the State Governmen t, all 33 districts of the State, \nincluding Dausa and Ganganagar are proposed to be i ncluded under PMGSY-III scheme. The \nState has recently submitted first batch of proposa ls of road length 2,839.13 km for \nconsideration by the Ministry of Rural Development. \n  \n********** \n \n \n \n \n\nANNEXURE-I \nAnnexure referred to in part (b) of Lok Sabha Starred Question No 25 to be answe