0 74460250 1528700 79630345 1574915 85657365 1617105 \n \n*Figures for 2017 is repeated for 2018 \n \n******* \n\nANNEXURE-II \n \nSTATEMENT IN REPLY TO PARTS (d ) & (e) OF THE LOK SABHA UNSTARRED \nQUESTION NO.59 ANSWERED ON 03.02.2020 REGARDING INFLOW OF \nTOURISTS \n  \nStatus of travel advisories of various countries for its citizens on travel to \nIndia is as under: \n  \nSr. No. Name of the \nCountry \nContent of Travel Advisory in regard to CAA \n1. Australia Be alert, monitor local media and follow the \ninstructions of local authorities. \n2. Belgium General advisory. \n3. Canada Issued a safety and security notice in view \nof demonstration against new Citizenship \nlegislation. \n4. China Issued an advisory for Chinese citizens in \nIndia to give priority to their safety and \nsecurity and avoid areas of demonstration \n5. Malaysia General advisory to be vigilant and give \nutmost priority to their personal safety and \nsecurity. \n6. New Zealand Advised New Zealanders to exercise \nincrease caution. \n7. UK Advised to exercise caution, monitor local \nmedia for the latest information, follow \ninstructions of the local authorities and \nallow more time for travel \n8. USA There is no active travel advisory or  travel \nwarning at this time \n \n \n******* ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_6": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \nDEPARTMENT OF HIGHER EDUCATION \n \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 6  \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2020 \n \nStudy in India \n \n6.  DR. (PROF.) KIRIT PREMJIBHAI SOLANKI:  \n \n Will the Minister of HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT be pleased to state: \n  \n(a) the salient features of “Study in India” programme announced in the budget;  \n(b) the number of students from other countries who are studying in various Indian \nUniversities and colleges under this programme;   \n(c) the details of the countries of origin of students from abroad studying in India; and  \n(d) the State-wise/UT-wise number of foreign students studying in Indian institutions? \n   \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF HUMAN RESOURCE DEVELOPMENT \n(SHRI RAMESH POKHRIYAL ‘NISHANK’) \n \n(a):    To facilitate Internationalization of Higher Education in India, a programme viz. \n‘Study in India’ was launched with the objectives to make India an education hub for \nforeign students; improve the soft power of India with focu s on the neighbouring countries \nand use it as a tool in diplomacy; to rapidly increase the inflow of inbound International \nStudents in India through a systematic brand -building, marketing, social media and digital \nmarketing campaigns; to increase India’s m arket share of global education exports; \nimprovement in overall quality of higher education; to reduce the export -import imbalance \nin the number of international students; growth in India’s global market share of \nInternational students; and increase in glo bal ranking of India etc.   The salient features of \nthe scheme include:  \na. Identification of target 30+ countries for branding in initial phase  \nb. Selection of top 100 partner institutions on the basis of  grading given by \nNational Assessment and Accreditation Council(NAAC)(3.26+) and ranking \nunder National Institutional Ranking Framework (NIRF)  \nc. Creation of a dedicated web portal www.studyindia.gov.in \nd. Setting up of call centre support \ne. Systematic branding  \n\nf. Undertaking of social media and offline advertisements campaigns  \ng. Fee waivers upto 100% being offered by partner institutions \nh. Adequate scholarships to meritorious students through IND-SAT Examination  \ni. Conduct of event management in the target countries \nj. Conduct of Webinars \nk. Setting up of Hostels of International Standards \nl. Study in India Mobile Application \nm. Conduct of event management in the target countries \nn. Conduct of National/ regional workshops to sensitize the partner institutes on \ninternationalization requirement \n \n(b)   The number of students studying in various Indian Universities and colleges is 768 and \n3164 respectively for Admission Cycles 2019 and 2020.  \n \n(c)   As per All India Survey on Higher Education 2018 -19, t he country-wise details of \nInternational students studying in India is at Annexure-I.  \n \n(d)  As per All India Survey on Higher Education 2018 -19, t he State -wise/UT-wise \nnumber of foreign students studying in Indian institutions is at Annexure-II.  \n \n***** \n  \n\nANNEXURE-I \nANNEXURE-I REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PART (c ) OF LOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 6 ASKED BY DR. (PROF.) KIRIT PREMJIBHAI \nSOLANKI, MP, LOK SABHA TO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2020 REGARDING \n‘STUDY IN INDIA’ \nCOUNTRY-WISE INTERNATIONAL STUDENTS \nSL. NO. COUNTRY NO. OF STUDENTS \n1 NEPAL 12747 \n2 AFGHANISTAN 4657 \n3 BANGLADESH 2075 \n4 SUDAN 1905 \n5 BHUTAN 1811 \n6 NIGERIA 1614 \n7 UNITED STATES 1518 \n8 YEMEN 1498 \n9 SRI LANKA 1252 \n10 IRAN 1127 \n11 MALAYSIA 1087 \n12 UNITED ARAB EMIRATES 1050 \n13 TANZANIA 968 \n14 ETHIOPIA 870 \n15 SOMALIA 670 \n16 CANADA 527 \n17 IRAQ 498 \n18 TIBETAN REFUGEES 492 \n19 KENYA 489 \n20 MYANMAR 479 \n21 ZAMBIA 475 \n22 SAUDI ARABIA 470 \n23 ZIMBABWE 467 \n24 SYRIAN ARAB REPUBLIC 453 \n25 THAILAND 398 \n26 CONGO 379 \n27 OMAN 361 \n28 QATAR 356 \n29 KUWAIT 338 \n30 BAHRAIN 284 