    "ls|LS17_S3_U_60": "     \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA                                                                                                            \nMINISTRY OF RAILWAYS \n \n \nLOK SABHA                                                                                                                                  \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 60                                                                                                               \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 05.02.2020 \n \nSURVEY OF THALASSERY-MYSURU RAILWAY LINE \n \n \n*60.   SHRI K. MURALEEDHARAN:  \n    \n      \n          Will the Minister of RAILWAYS be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the survey on the Thalassery-Mysuru railway line has been \nstopped and if so, the reasons therefor; \n \n(b) whether it is a fact that Railways has almost shelved the Nilambur -\nNanjangud railway line project and if so, the reasons therefor; \n \n(c) whether the revised Thalassery -Mysuru project had been the only \nhope for the people of Malabar for connecting Mysuru and \nBengaluru directly through a railway line; and \n \n(d) if so, the steps taken by the Railways to restore the work of \nThalassery-Mysuru railway line survey at the earliest? \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n    ANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF RAILWAYS AND COMMERCE & INDUSTRY \n \n   (SHRI PIYUSH GOYAL) \n   \n(a)  to (d)  A Statement is laid on the Table of the House. \n \n***** \n \n \n \n\n  \n \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d) OF STARRED \nQUESTION NO. 60 BY SHRI K. MURALEEDHARAN TO BE ANSWERED IN \nLOK SABHA ON 05.02.2020 REGARDING SURVEY OF THALASSERY -\nMYSURU RAILWAY LINE \n \n(a), (c) &  (d): The work of Thalassery -Mysuru railway line is a part of  the \nbasket of projects identified by Kerala State Government and entrusted to \nKerala Rail Development Corpor ation Limited (KRDCL). The Survey work \nfor the above project was entrusted to M/s Konkan Railway Corporation \nLimited for preparing the Detailed Project Report (DPR) . KRDCL have \nsubmitted the Pre -Feasibility Report on the above Project by proposing \nthe alignment via Kutta (Madikeri District in Karnataka) to Railway Board. \nRailway Board has advised for obtaining Forest Clearance and alignment \nwith approval of all the Stake Holders. Government of Kerala has \nrequested for a high level meeting between Kerala & K arnataka States at \nChief Secretary level along with officials concerned from Forest \nDepartment and Transport Department for approving the alignment  as \nalignment is passing through the States of Kerala and Karnataka. DPR will \nbe finalised in light of the outcome of the above mentioned meeting. \n \n \n(b): Kerala Rail Development Corporation Limited has been entrusted for \npreparation of Detailed Project Report (DPR) of the work of Nilambur –\nNanjangud Rail Line Project by Government of Kerala. DPR of this Project \nwill also be finalised in light of the outcome of high level meeting between \nKerala & Karnataka States at Chief Secretary level along with officials \nconcerned from Forest Department and Transp ort Department as \nalignment is passing through the States of Kerala and Karnataka. \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_61": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(DEPARTMENT OF SPORTS) \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. 61 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 06.02.2020 \n \nDay Boarding Centres \n \n†*61.  SHRI RAHUL KASWAN: \n \nWill the Minister of YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS be pleased to \nstate: \n \n(a) the details of the process for setting up of day boarding centres by \nthe Sports Authority of India; \n(b) the facilities being/proposed to be provided to the players and \ninstitutions in such centres; \n(c) the number of day boarding centres set up in Rajasthan during the \nlast five years, sport-wise and district-wise; and \n(d) the details of the kit and the quantum of funds provided to the day \nboarding centres and players from time to time in Rajasthan during the \nlast five years? \n \nANSWER \n \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) \nFOR YOUTH AFFAIRS AND SPORTS \n(SHRI KIREN RIJIJU) \n \n(a) to (d) A statement is laid on the table of the House. \n \n  \n\nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN REPLY TO PARTS (a) TO (d ) OF THE LOK \nSABHA STARRED QUESTION No. 61 FOR 06/02/2020  ASKED B Y SH. \nRAHUL KASWAN REGARDING DAY BOARDING CENTRES. \n \n \n \nThe Sports Authority of India (SAI) does not set up Day Boarding \nCentres.  SAI runs Regional Training Centres, SAI Training Centres and \nNational Institute of Sports (NIS), Patiala.  These SAI training facilities \nare available to residential as well as non -residential athletes selected \nunder various sports promotion schemes of the Department of Sports and \nSAI.  In the State of Rajasthan, SAI is running its training centres at \nJodhpur, Alwar and Jaipur.  In these 3 SAI Training Centres, a total of 231 \nathletes are benefitting which includes 104 day boarders.  \n \n***** \n ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_62": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 62 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2020 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT IN RURAL AREAS \n \n62.  SHRIMATI PRATIMA MONDAL:  \n \n Will the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP \nbe pleased to state:  \n \n(a)  whether the Government has taken any step to e nsure and promote skill \ndevelopment in rural areas of the country;  \n(b)  whether the Government ensures job after the c ourse of skill development is \nfinished; and  \n(c)  the details of candidates who have been benefi ted from the schemes in the \nrural areas, State-wise? \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP  \n(SHRI R. K. SINGH)  \n \n(a) to (c)  Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (20 16 - 2020) is the flagship \noutcome-based Skill Training Scheme of the Ministry  of Skill Development & \nEntrepreneurship (MSDE) which aims to train 10 mill ion youths by 2020 pan India \nboth in Rural and Urban areas.   MSDE does not main tain any segregated data for \nrural and urban areas. There are three training rou tes under the scheme: Short term \nTraining for fresh skilling of school / college dro p outs and unemployed youth, \nRecognition of Prior Learning (RPL) to recognize th e existing skills and Special \nProjects to address skilling requirements of groups  which are under represented or \nrequire special initiatives and efforts. RPL only p rovides orientation to the already \nskilled workforce, and does not mandate placements.  \n  \n Under PMKVY 2016-2020, Training Centres make all ef forts to facilitate \nplacements of certified candidates through multiple  initiatives like Rojgar Melas and \ncollaboration with industries and Sector Skill Coun cil. Also, candidates can avail \nbenefit of placement through ‘Yuva Sampark’ portal which brings both candidate and \npotential employer on IT platform to find potential  match between two (employer and \ncandidate). \n \n The details of candidates who have been benefited under PMKVY as on \n17th Jan 2020, data reported in Systematic Data Management System reports is at  \n \n \n\n \n Directorate General of Training (DGT) under MSDE i s entrusted with the \nresponsibility of long term vocational training in the Country. One of the flagship \nschemes is ‘Craftsmen Training Scheme’ being implem ented through network of \n15,042 Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs)  (Govt . 2738 + Private 12,304 ITIs) located \nall over the country with an objective to provide s killed work force to the industry in \n138 trades with duration of 6 months , 1 year and 2  year . Initiatives for improving \nquality of ITIs include, formulation of new affilia tion norms, grading to evaluate their \nperformance, ISO 29990 certification to raise the o verall quality and standards, \nregular inspection of ITIs, regular up-gradation of training content of ITI curriculum as \nper industrial requirement etc. The details of the candidates who have been \nbenefited under Craftsmen Training Scheme are at Annexure-II. \n \nMinistry of Rural Development is implementing Deen Dayal Upadhyaya \nGrameen Kaushalya Yojana (DDU-GKY), a placement lin ked skill development \nprogram for rural poor youth under National Rural L ivelihoods Mission (NRLM) all \nover the country. Every candidate undergoing traini ng under DDU-GKY is given \nmandatory basic training in Information Technology for 80 Hours. During the year \n2019-20 (upto 31st October, 2019) 1,27,918 candidates have been provided training. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure-I  \nAnnexure as referred to in reply of Part (a) & (c) of Lok Sabha Question No. 62 \ndated 03.02.2020 regarding ‘SKILL DEVELOPMENT IN RURAL AREAS’ \nPMKVY 2016-20 State/UT wise Progress as per SDMS Reports till 17-Jan-\n2020 \n  STT SPL RPL \nState / UT   Trained   \nReported \nPlaced \n  \nTrained \n 