    "ls|LS17_S3_U_63": "GOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF FINANCE \nDEPARTMENT OF REVENUE \nLOK SABHA \nUNSTARRED QUESTION No. 63 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON MONDAY, FEBRUARY 3, 2020/MAGHA 14, 1941 (SAKA) \n \nFILING OF GST RETURNS \n \n63.  SHRI P. C. GADDIGOUDAR: \n \nWill the Minister of FINANCE be pleased to state: \n \n(a) whether the Government is aware that a large number of traders, micro, small and medium \nenterprises are facing lots of difficulties in filing their Goods and Services Tax (GST) Returns;  \n(b) if so, whe ther the Government has any proposal to set up facilitation centres on the lines of \nAadhaar Seva Kendras to help them in filing their returns; and \n(c) if so, the details thereof and the time by which such centres are likely to be set up?  \n \nANSWER \nMINISTER OF STATE FOR FINANCE (SHRI ANURAG SINGH THAKUR) \n \n(a) The Government is committed to ease the process for filing of returns under GST for all \ntaxpayers, including traders, micro, small and medium enterprises. Outreach programs to create \nawareness about retu rn filing among small taxpayers have been carried out across the country. \nBesides, the following initiatives have also been taken up to further simplify return filing process \nfor small taxpayers: \ni. Taxpayers whose annual turnover is less than 1.5 crore ru pees have the option to file return \nin FORM GSTR-1 on a quarterly basis, instead of monthly basis. \nii. An option has been provided to the composition taxpayers for filing of FORM GSTR -4 on \nan annual basis, instead of quarterly basis. \niii. Filing of annual return in FORM GSTR -9 and reconciliation statement in FORM GSTR -\n9C for financial years 2017 -18 and 2018 -19 has been made optional for small taxpayers whose \naggregate turnover in the preceding financial year did not exceed two crore rupees. \niv. The new retu rn model under GST envisages quarterly filing of return for those taxpayers \nwhose aggregate annual turnover does not exceed five crore rupees. \n \n(b) and (c) GST Seva Kendras have already been set up in various Central Tax offices to assist the \ntaxpayers. However, at this stage, there is no proposal for setting up facilitation centres on the \nlines of Aadhaar Seva Kendras.  \n \n***** ",
    "ls|LS17_S3_U_64": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \nLOK SABHA \nSTARRED QUESTION NO. *64 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON FEBRUARY 06, 2020 \nHOUSING FOR URBAN POOR  \n \nNO.  *64.  SHRI ASADUDDIN OWAISI: \nSHRI SYED IMTIAZ JALEEL: \n \nWill the Minister of HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS be pleased \nto state: \n(a) whether the scheme of housing for urban poorund er Pradhan \nMantri Awas Yojana (Urban) was launchedin June 2015  with the aim \nto build 1.12 crore houses; \n(b) if so, the total number of houses handed over t othe beneficiaries \nso far and the steps taken to achieve thesaid target; \n(c) whether the Government has recently sanctioned 6.5 lakh \nhouses under the scheme and if so, the detailsthereof, State-wise; \n(d) the total funds released by the Government unde r the scheme to \nthe States; and \n(e) the cost sharing ratio of Centre and States underthe Scheme? \n \nANSWER \nTHE MINISTER OF STATE (INDEPENDENT CHARGE) OF THE \nMINISTRY OF HOUSING AND URBAN AFFAIRS \n \n[SHRI HARDEEP SINGH PURI] \n***** \n \n \n(a) to (e):  A statement is laid on the Table of th e Sabha. \n \n \nContd…2/ \n \n\n \n-2- \nSTATEMENT REFERRED TO IN THE LOK SABHA STARRED \nQUESTION NO. *64 DUE FOR 06.02.2020 REGARDING  \n“HOUSING FOR URBAN POOR” \n \n \n \n(a)  & (b):  Pradhan Mantri Awas Yojana (Urban) [PMAY(U) ] was \nlaunched on 25.06.2015 for addressing the housing r equirement of \nthe people belonging to Economically Weaker Section  (EWS), Lower \nIncome Group (LIG) and Middle Income Group (MIG) ca tegories in \nurban areas.States/UTs have undertaken demand surve y under the \nscheme for assessing actual demand of housing.  The  validated \ndemand reported by States/UTs so far is around 1.12 crore.   \nBased on the project proposals received so far from  the States/UTs, \na total 1,03,22,560 houses have been sanctioned und er the Scheme; \nout of this, 60,50,991 are at various stages of con struction and \n32,07,573 are completed/delivered.   \nFurther, States/UTs have been requested to get the project \nproposals for all their remaining demand of houses sanctioned by \nMarch, 2020 so that construction of all houses may progressively be \ncompleted by 2022.  \n \n(c): Yes, Sir.  A total 6,70,239 houses were sancti oned in the \nmonth of December, 2019. State/UT-wise details are at annexure - I. \n \n(d):  Central Assistance of Rs. 63,676.50 crore has  been \nreleased so farto the States/UTs under the scheme. \n \n \nContd…3/ \n \n\n \n-3- \n \n(e) Central Government provides different levels of  financial \nassistance under following four verticals of the Scheme: \nS. \nNo. \nVertical Central Assistance per house \n1. In-situ Slum \nRedevelopment (ISSR) \nRs. 1.00 lakh \n2. Credit Linked Subsidy \nScheme (CLSS) \nInterest subsidy of 6.5%, 4% and 3% \non housing loan amounts upto Rs. 6 \nlakh, Rs. 9 lakh and Rs. 12 \nlakhrespectively for beneficiaries \nbelonging to Economical Weaker \nSection (EWS)/Lower Income Group \n(LIG), Middle Income Group-I (MIG-I) \nand MIG-II categories.\n \n3. Affordable Housing in \nPartnership (AHP) \nRs. 1.50 lakh \n4. Beneficiary-led individual \nhouse construction/ \nenhancements (BLC) \nRs. 1.50 lakh \n \nCentral Assistance under PMAY(U) for different vert icals is fixed for \nall States/UTs notwithstanding topographical/geogra phical \ndifferences across the country.  Further, States/UT s also make \ndifferent levels of financial assistance to the ben eficiaries under \nAHP and BLC verticals of the scheme.  State/UT-wise  details are at \nAnnexure – II. \n***** \n \n \n \n \n \n\n \nAnnexure I referred in reply to LSSQ No 64 due for 06-02-2020 \n \n \nState/ UT wise details of Central assistance and Ho uses Sanctioned recently during the \nmonth of December 2019 under PMAY(U) \n \n \nS. No. \n \nState Central Assistance \nSanctioned (Rs. in Cr) \nNumber of Houses \nSanctioned \n1 A&N Island (UT)  - - \n2 Andhra Pradesh  5,574.50 3,71,184 \n3 Arunachal Pradesh  - - \n4 Assam