    "ls|LS17_S3_U_75": " \nGOVERNMENT OF INDIA \nMINISTRY OF SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n \nLOK SABHA \n \nUNSTARRED QUESTION NO. 75 \nTO BE ANSWERED ON 03.02.2020 \n \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT TO YOUTH OF OTHER BACKWARD CLASS \n \n75. SHRI RAJESH VERMA: \n \nWill the Minister of SKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRE NEURSHIP be \npleased to state : \n \n(a) the number of youths of backward classes/extrem ely backward classes benefited \nunder the skill development scheme across the country during the last three years; \n \n(b) the details thereof along with the number of yo uths of backward classes/ \nextremely backward classes benefited under this sch eme particularly in Sitapur district \nof Uttar Pradesh; \n \n(c) the total number of skill development centres o pened so far in Uttar Pradesh; and \n \n(d) the details thereof, district-wise? \n \n     \nANSWER \n \nMINISTER OF STATE IN THE MINISTRY OF  \nSKILL DEVELOPMENT AND ENTREPRENEURSHIP \n(SHRI R.K. SINGH) \n \n \n \n(a) Under Ministry of Skill Development and Entrepr eneurship (MSDE’s) flagship \nscheme Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY 2 .0) 2016-20 as on 17 \nth  \nJanuary, 2020, more than 73 lakh candidates have be en trained across the country out \nof which more than 21 lakh candidates belong to OBC  category. Year wise details of \nnumber of OBC candidates trained/oriented, certifie d and placed under PMKVY are at \nAnnexure-I.  \n  \nFurther, in long term training imparted through Ind ustrial Training Institutes (ITIs), \nthere is a provision for reservation of seats for t raining of candidates belonging to \nOBCs. During last three years (2017-19), a total of  18,22,787 OBC candidates have \nbeen imparted training through ITIs in various trades across the country.  \n \n  \n \n\n \n \nMinistry of Social Justice and Empowerment through National Backward Classes \nFinance and Development Corporation (NBCFDC) also f acilitates skill development \ntraining to its target group including OBCs. Year-w ise details of OBC candidates trained \nby Ministry of Social Justice are placed at Annexure-II. \n \n(b) Under PMKVY (2016-2020), as on 17 \nth  January, 2020, a total of 2848 OBC \ncandidates have been trained in Sitapur district of  Uttar Pradesh. Year wise details of \nnumber of OBC candidates trained/oriented, certifie d and placed under PMKVY in \nSitapur district of Uttar Pradesh are at Annexure-III. \n During last three years (2017-19), a total of 2610  OBC candidates have been \nimparted training through ITIs in Sitapur district of Uttar Pradesh. \n(c) & (d) Under PMKVY as on 17 th  January 2020, 1721 training centres were \nimparting training in the State of Uttar Pradesh. T here are 3229 ITIs in the State of Uttar \nPradesh. The district wise details of training centres and ITIs are at Annexure-IV.  \n  \n\nAnnexure-I \n  \nAnnexure referred to in reply to LSUQ No. 75 to be answered on 03.02.2020 asked \nby SHRI RAJESH VERMA regarding ‘SKILL DEVELOPMENT T O YOUTH OF \nOTHER BACKWARD CLASS’ \nPMKVY 2016-20-CSCM-OBC Progress as per SDMS Reports till 17-Jan-2020 \n \nFY    Trained / Oriented  Certified  Reported Placed  \nShort Term Training (STT) \nFY-16-17 15,714 3,090 86 \nFY-17-18 5,75,467 4,21,818 1,60,449 \nFY-18-19 3,02,164 3,12,836 2,31,984 \nFY-19-20 2,96,385 2,42,906 1,44,417 \nSTT-Total 11,89,730 9,80,650 5,36,936 \nSpecial Project (SP) \nFY-16-17 313 22 0 \nFY-17-18 7,499 4,546 1,932 \nFY-18-19 13,708 9,637 4,965 \nFY-19-20 19,814 15,177 6,837 \nSPL-Total 41,334 29,382 13,734 \nRecognition of Prior Learning (RPL) \nFY-16-17 80,649 37,169 NA \nFY-17-18 1,70,515 1,51,690 NA \nFY-18-19 2,69,901 1,49,439 NA \nFY-19-20 3,68,679 3,56,016 NA \nRPL -Total  8,89,744  6,94,314  NA  \nGrand Total 21,20,808 17,04,346 5,50,670 \n  \n  \n\nAnnexure-II  \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to LSUQ No. 75 to be answered on 03.02.2020 asked \nby SHRI RAJESH VERMA regarding ‘SKILL DEVELOPMENT T O YOUTH OF \nOTHER BACKWARD CLASS’ \n \nDetails of training of OBC candidates done by Ministry of Social Justice and \nEmpowerment   \nYear No. of trainees \n2016-17 18748 \n2017-18 23380 \n2018-19 25040 \n2019-20 33149 \nTotal 100317 \n  \n\nAnnexure-III \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to LSUQ No. 75 to be answered on 03.02.2020 asked \nby SHRI RAJESH VERMA regarding ‘SKILL DEVELOPMENT T O YOUTH OF \nOTHER BACKWARD CLASS’ \nPMKVY 2016-20-CSCM-OBC Progress in Sitapur District as per SDMS \nReports till 17-Jan-2020 \n \nFY  Trained / Oriented  Certified  Reported Placed  \nShort Term Training (STT)  \nFY-16-17 0 0 0 \nFY-17-18 1,273 969 443 \nFY-18-19 553 640 525 \nFY-19-20 613 386 206 \nSTT-Total 2,439 1,995 1,174 \nSpecial Project (SP)  \nFY-16-17 0 0 0 \nFY-17-18 0 0 0 \nFY-18-19 0 0 0 \nFY-19-20 44 42 0 \nSPL-Total 44 42 0 \nRecognition of Prior Learning (RPL)  \nFY-16-17 0 0 NA \nFY-17-18 0 0 NA \nFY-18-19 317 143 NA \nFY-19-20 48 86 NA \nRPL -Total  365  229  0 \nGrand Total 2,848 2,266 1,174 \n \n \n \n \n  \n\nAnnexure-IV \n \nAnnexure referred to in reply to LSUQ No. 75 to be answered on 03.02.2020 asked \nby SHRI RAJESH VERMA regarding ‘SKILL DEVELOPMENT T O YOUTH OF \nOTHER BACKWARD CLASS’ \nSkill Development Centres in Uttar Pradesh \nDistrict  ITIs Count PMKVY Training Centres  \nAgra 132 89 \nAligarh 69 43 \nAllahabad 204 38 \nAmbedkar Nagar 61 12 \nAmethi 20 7 \nAmroha 13 15 \nAuraiya 11 23 \nAzamgarh 136 11 \nBadaun 14 11 \nBaghpat 17 4 \nBahraich 7 6 \nBallia 82 19 \nBalrampur 5 5 \nBanda 11 7 \nBarabanki 28 14 \nBareilly 33 63 \nBasti 25 11 \nBijnor 21 50 \nBulandshahr 42 31 \nChandauli 43 16 \nChitrakoot 8 4 \nDeoria 61 17 \nEtah 28 20 \nEtawah 12 31 \nFaizabad 96 17 \nFarrukhabad 14 13 \nFatehpur 18 17 \nFirozabad 43 44 \nGautam Buddha Nagar 32 34 \nGhaziabad 32 59 \nGhazipur 184 22 \nGonda 17 11 \nGorakhpur 144 46 \nHamirpur 8 11 \nHapur 28 11 \nHardoi 11 15 \nHathras 47 24 \nJalaun 17 22 \n\nJaunpur 136 32 \nJhansi 54 16 \nKannauj 6 12 \nKanpur Dehat 16 18 \nKanpur Nagar 77 89 \nKanshiram Nagar 5 19 \nKausham